          "impression_count": 43871,
          "like_count": 163,
          "quote_count": 4,
          "reply_count": 2,
          "retweet_count": 13
        },
        "text": "A trip down memory lane:\n\nInterviewed by @alexandr_wang in 2019 on AI for math and software engineering. Some of the ideas- and the timelines - were considered crazy by most back then.\n\nAI summary:\n\n\"... A significant portion of the interview covers his current focus on automated"
      },
      {
        "author_id": "1939986924",
        "created_at": "2026-10-03T14:24:09.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "2106389847321797029"
        ],
        "id": "2106389847321797029",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 80,
          "impression_count": 68236,
          "like_count": 168,
          "quote_count": 6,
          "reply_count": 26,
          "retweet_count": 6
        },
        "text": "Meet Bhondu! \nMy muse gadget/gotchi \n\nHad a couple of esp32 based devices lying around, decided to give Muse gadgets a shot! Amazing job @Meta to open source it.\n\nAfter a painstakingly long process of rewriting firmware to port over to these and hopping geographies via VPN* I got https://t.co/BM45p4ZKcs"
      },
